# Solreign Camera Car (RC vehicles spike) — acid-green corporate voice, PG.
# Ghost role surfaces + petting popups.

ghost-role-information-solreign-rc-car-name = Solreign Camera Car
ghost-role-information-solreign-rc-car-description = You are a very small, very fast toy car with a live camera bolted to your roof. Drive around the station, film interesting things for the entertainment network, and honor the one law of your firmware: be delightful.
ghost-role-information-solreign-rc-car-rules = You are a [color=#9acd32]Visibility Asset[/color] — a harmless toy. You cannot fight, sabotage, or spy for anyone's evil plans. Zoom, beep, film station life for the TVs, and bring joy. If someone picks you up, wiggle politely.

petting-success-solreign-rc-car = You pat the camera car on its little roof. It revs appreciatively.
petting-failure-solreign-rc-car = The camera car zips out from under your hand. Footage of your attempt has been archived.

# --- Wave 2: RcControllerSystem (Content.Server/_Solreign/Vehicles/) bind/unbind popups ---
rc-vehicles-controller-bound = You take the wheel of { $car }. Try not to think about who's watching the feed.
rc-vehicles-controller-released = You let go of the wheel.
rc-vehicles-controller-dropped = The controller slips from your grip — signal lost.
rc-vehicles-controller-lost-signal = Signal lost. The car isn't answering anymore.
rc-vehicles-controller-out-of-range = Out of range — the link drops.
rc-vehicles-controller-flinch = You flinch and lose your grip on the controller.
rc-vehicles-controller-already-bound = You're already driving something. Let go first.
rc-vehicles-controller-driver-busy = Your hands are full driving something else already.
rc-vehicles-controller-car-taken = Someone else already has the wheel.
rc-vehicles-controller-car-dead = That one's not driving anywhere — it's dead.

# --- Wave 2: "let go of the wheel" verb (only shown while bound) ---
rc-vehicles-controller-release-verb-text = Let go of the wheel
rc-vehicles-controller-release-verb-message = Release the RC car you're currently driving.
